      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a mute player who uses the chatbox all the time, I don't think this is a good idea for a couple reasons:\n\nIt kind of interferes with an accessibility feature. If I'm trying to communicate to another player using the chatbox, the NPC in the world would also react. Both ideas can already be done with in-world text boxes, see worlds like Audience Anarchy and Who Said What.\n\nAnd then there's the privacy concerns with worlds having direct access to what you're typing. It could be potentially abused to log people's messages to an external url. It's the same reason why worlds shouldn't have direct access to what people are saying through voice chat.\n\nThe chatbox should be exclusively used for chatting with other players imo.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
