      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It will actually grant new accessibility features. If you are doing a TED talk, you want to present to an audience, Udon can amplify your voice, but there is no equivalent function for a mute person using Chatbox. This will allow that.\n\nYou don't have to worry about privacy, worlds cannot dynamically create urls to load or otherwise upload data to any external server. (By the way, VRChat already logs your Chatbox messages)\n\nIf you are chatting with another player using Chatbox, some random player can also readily react to it, so there is no privacy concern. Having NPCs able to react to it is an accessibility feature allowing a NEW mechanism of interacting with the world with \"chat\". It does not replace the text boxes where you need to have a certain input like Audience Anarchy because those are a different use case where you want it to be private message.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-25T20:29:04.695Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "bool `VRCPlayerApi.Chatbox.IsTyping`\n\nstring `VRCPlayerApi.Chatbox.Text`\n\nThis opens up possibilities for chatting (with text) as a way to interact with the world, e.g. NPCs responding to certain keywords you are \"speaking\".\n\nOr world specific custom placement of Chatboxes. Maybe someone wants to do a presentation and needs their Chatbox enlarged for a large audience. This will be equivalent to player audio setting a higher voice gain.\n\nThis allows chatting to be an actual game mechanic in VRChat.",
